    "body": "Closes #259\n\nReal `IRefundService` (contract `payments.md` 3.4, P2) and Booking's `AssignmentFailed` handling (`booking.md` section 5).\n\n**Schema change SC-10 (needs M1's eye):** `PAYMENT_TRANSACTION` gets `refunded_amount DECIMAL(18,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0`, `refund_reason NVARCHAR(255) NULL`, `refunded_at DATETIME2 NULL` (entity `PaymentTransaction.cs`, its configuration, ONE migration `20261010021307_AddPaymentRefundColumns` generated with `dotnet ef migrations add` in the .NET 10 SDK container; the snapshot diff is these three properties only; the migration is up/down of exactly three columns). Recorded in `.spec/decisions.md` (SC-10, Q24). This is the leader's recommended default for P2; the approval was **relayed by M2 from private messages and is not yet confirmed on GitHub**: Kiệt is asked to confirm on #259.\n**The migration was NOT applied to a database** (SQL Server unreachable in the author's session): `dotnet ef database update` and a real insert/refund are unverified.\n\n- `RefundService` replaces `FakeRefundService` (registered by `PaymentsModule`): refunds against the order's SUCCESS / partly REFUNDED ORDER transaction; amount via `Vnd.Round`, > 0 and <= `amount - refunded_amount`; the refund is **reserved in the database first** with one conditional `UPDATE ... WHERE status IN (SUCCESS, REFUNDED) AND refunded_amount + :amount <= amount` (concurrent refunds cannot exceed the paid amount), then `IPaymentGateway.RefundAsync`; a refusal or an error reverts the reservation exactly (status back to SUCCESS when nothing remains refunded). A gateway without a refund API is recorded in the database only and the result message says so. Then `OrderRefunded` and a `payment.status` push; a failing listener never turns a done refund into a failure.\n- `AssignmentFailedHandler` (Booking): a PAID / DISPATCHING / ASSIGNED order -> CANCELLED (`cancel_reason` = the event's reason, 255 max), `OrderCancelled`, then a 100 % refund of `total_amount`; an order already cancelled, unpaid, completed or unknown is left alone, so a repeat is not refunded twice. Dispatch never touches the order status (checked by grep), so this handler is the only place the order is cancelled.\n- Callers that already use `IRefundService` with partial amounts (`AbsenceReportService.cs:144`, `DisputeVerdictService.cs:99`) now hit the real service: partial refunds work and are recorded (this is why P2 was needed).\n\nVerification: **local `verify L3` could not run** (Windows Smart App Control blocks the freshly built unsigned `CommonService.dll`, see the comment on #250). Backend tests ran in the official `mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:10.0` Linux container: `Passed! - Failed: 0, Passed: 1553, Skipped: 0, Total: 1553`. New tests: `Backend/Tests/Payments/RefundServiceTests.cs` (full, partial + second partial, exact remaining and one dong more, non-positive, rounding, unknown / unpaid / expired, gateway refusal and error revert, failed second refund keeps the first, DB-only path, concurrent refunds, reason truncation, failing listener) and `Backend/Tests/Booking/AssignmentFailedHandlerTests.cs`. The harness gate is this PR's CI `verify-l3`.\n**Not verified / known gaps:**\n- No DB-backed test: the conditional `ExecuteUpdateAsync` reserve/revert and the migration are untested against SQL Server (the in-memory repository mimics their semantics with a lock).\n- A failed refund after `AssignmentFailed` is only logged as an error (no retry mechanism): the order stays cancelled and must be refunded by hand.\n- The Premium capacity hold is not released on cancel (Scope exception #257).\n- Revert is two statements run in one transaction; the revert itself can fail (it would then leave the refund recorded without the gateway having paid).\n- Not in this PR (as the ticket says): P4 late-payment refund, B4 PAID -> DISPATCHING, extension refund (BE-M2-08), customer cancel (BE-M2-09).\nChecklist: BE-M2-07 ticked in `.spec/plan/M2-booking-payments.md`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
